tt-local-generator (0.61.4) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(create): the pending result card kept resizing while a job ran. The
    status label (updated by progress messages) and the elapsed label (ticking
    every second) had unbounded natural widths, so each text change nudged the
    two-pane layout. Both are now bounded/centered (status caps at 40 chars and
    wraps in place; elapsed is centered) and the card gets a min-width floor, so
    a running job's changing text re-wraps in place instead of jittering the
    card size.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Sun, 03 Aug 2026 17:45:00 +0000

tt-local-generator (0.61.3) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(create): the result pane jumped BELOW the form once generation started
    (most visible with AnimateDiff's wide/tall options). Root cause was pure
    size negotiation in the two-pane FlowBox: (1) the pending card's prompt
    Gtk.Label wrapped but had no max-width-chars, so its natural width was the
    full un-wrapped prompt (~1000px), ballooning the result pane; and (2) a wide
    medium form sprawled its natural width past the intended ~660px column. Both
    are now bounded — the prompt label caps at 48 chars, and the form column is
    wrapped in a MaxWidthBin(720) — so the result pane keeps its side slot on a
    wide window and only stacks below on a genuinely narrow one.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Sun, 03 Aug 2026 17:20:00 +0000

tt-local-generator (0.61.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(create): the Video → AnimateDiff "Frame count" control rendered as one
    giant stretched input — in the Controls FlowBox it shared a wrap-line with
    the tall "AnimateDiff Options" group and its default valign=FILL stretched
    it. Control rows are now anchored valign=START so each keeps its natural
    height.
  * feat(create): the Direction zone's "+N more…" disclosure is now a compact
    inline pill beside the visible chips instead of its own full-width row per
    category (reclaims a line for every chip category).
  * feat(create): the collapsed "Controls" expander now advertises what's
    inside (e.g. "Controls — Steps, Seed, Frame count, …") instead of a bare
