tt-local-generator (0.61.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(create): the model door's Wan2.2-Animate card was a silent dead end —
    `_server_key_to_medium_id` had no rule for the "animate" capability once
    Task 2 removed the native "animate" medium, so the click resolved to no
    medium and no-opped. It now folds onto "video" (mirroring how
    `_classify_server_key_for_model_door` already files Animate under the
    Video model-door group), so clicking the card lands on the Video medium
    with the Animate model preselected in the scoped dropdown.
  * fix(create): the scoped model dropdown's collapsed/selected button was
    still rendering the raw `ServerDef.label` implementation string (e.g.
    "Wan2.2-T2V-A14B  (P300X2)") even though the popped-open list already
    showed the friendly two-line name+benefit row. `_populate_model_dropdown`
    now builds the collapsed `Gtk.StringList` from
    `server_manager.display_name_for(key)` too, so no implementation string
    is ever shown to the user, in either dropdown state.
  * test: aligned `tests/test_create_view.py`'s `_fake_mediums()` with
    production `default_mediums()` (native = image + video only, no more
    stale native "animate" entry) — this fixture drift is what let the
    model-door dead-end above ship untested. Updated the tests that relied on
    the stale native-animate medium to use a local fixture instead, and added
    coverage for the Animate-door-card -> Video-medium routing fix.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 16:30:00 -0700

tt-local-generator (0.61.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * feat(create): "Video is Video" — the video trio (Wan2.2/Mochi/SkyReels,
    Wan2.2-Animate, and the AnimateDiff artgen generator) is one Video medium
    now, not three separate chips. Animate and AnimateDiff are *models* inside
    Video's scoped picker, selected the same way Wan2.2/Mochi/SkyReels are.
  * feat(server_manager): `benefit_for`/`display_name_for` seam — the Create
    model picker renders a friendly display name plus a short "what is this
    good for" benefit tagline for every model/server key, including the
    synthetic no-server `animatediff` entry.
  * feat(create): AnimateDiff (local, no server to start) is the default Video
    model whenever nothing on the video/animate hardware group is already
    running — a job always has a same-instant path to a result.
  * feat(create): picking the Animate model reveals Video's on-demand "Animate
    needs" section (motion video / character image / mode) inline; every other
    Video/Image job's `collect()` dict is unaffected.
  * feat(create): routes the Animate model through `_native_generate_args` to
    `AnimateGenerationWorker` (`model_source="animate"`), the same worker the
    old dedicated Animate chip used — no capability lost, no duplicated engine.
  * chore: existing artgen-`animatediff` records continue to render in the
    artgen gallery unchanged; this is a Create-surface taxonomy change only.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:48:58 -0700

tt-local-generator (0.60.4) noble; urgency=medium

  * ui(create): remove the redundant second "Prompt" box. Artgen generators that
    declare their own --prompt (AnimateDiff, Freeform, …) were surfacing a
    "Prompt" field in "Your brief" that duplicated — and was overridden by — the
    top "What do you want to make?" entry. RoleZonePanel now drops the prompt-key
    field (like it already drops model), so there is ONE prompt per medium; the
    generator's default still applies when the top entry is empty (collect()
    unchanged). An artgen medium whose only brief field was the prompt now hides
    its empty "Your brief" frame.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:15:28 -0700

